# scripts/lib/accept-s2-admin-agent-tickets.sh — S11 AA5c (the AA5 plan's §5.8 journey): in the
# trial workspace the admin agent scenario (accept-s2-admin-agent.sh) set up, the platform
# administrator's admin agent connects a test ticket system, looks at it, drafts what a ticket
# Worker needs and tries that Worker once; then proposes the same for the target workspace, which
# the person applies — on the real runtime (real pi in the admin container, its admin agent Handle,
# the admin mode of packages/platform-extension, llm-proxy in front of fake-llm, which scripts the
# five Turns: deploy/fake-llm/server.mjs `tickets*Scenario`). Run by scripts/accept_s2.sh in its
# fake-provider path right after `admin_agent_step` (`admin_agent_tickets_step`) and cleaned up by
# its cleanup_step (`admin_agent_tickets_cleanup`, before `admin_agent_cleanup`). Sourced after
# accept-s2-admin-agent.sh, whose globals and helpers (ADMIN_*, admin_cred, admin_cap) it uses;
# POSIX sh, same conventions (pass/fail, cap, parse_kv, run_driver, no temp file, no jq).
#
# The system: the openapi fixture's ticket book (deploy/accept-s2/openapi-fixture, `/tickets`,
# seeded with two tickets). Two ways to it, one credential each, both generated by accept_s2.sh:
#   - trial: its own gate, `accept-s2-tickets-gate` (docker-compose.yml) — started here, with the
#     connection secret minted in the trial workspace, because the trial workspace connects it on
#     its own (a gate answers only the secret it was started with); the credential is the run's
#     ACCEPT_S2_API_TOKEN, and the fixture records it on a ticket as `via: trial`;
#   - production: a gate-host instance the proposal's platform part creates; its shared credential
#     is ACCEPT_S2_TICKETS_PROD_TOKEN (`via: production`), entered as the console's 集成 page enters
#     one — to the gate host, never through the kernel (driver.mjs `gate-host-credential`).
# The fixture's `GET /tickets` names which credential read it (`readBy`), so a read through either
# gate shows the credential it holds without opening a ticket.
#
# The journey, five Turns of one admin agent Chat, the script playing the person in between:
#   A. the agent asks for the ticket system to be connected (`request_connection`, http,
#      `helpdesk`); the request records its session;
#      the person completes the request card: enters the test credential (`create_connection`
#      naming the request, the OpenAPI document as its manifest source), publishes the three
#      imported Operations as read (`publish_manifest`), grants the gate to themselves
#      (`connect_gatekeeper` — the console's Systems & access page, 系统与授权; without it the
#      Worker below could not ask for an action on the gate);
#   B. the agent finds the ticket Operations, observes `tickets.list` through its projected observe
#      tool (its execute tool is never offered to it), drafts two Skills and a Worker that may ask
#      for actions on that gate; the person publishes the three drafts in the trial workspace;
#   C. the agent tries the Worker (`invoke_worker`); the Worker's `tickets.create` waits for a
#      decision; the person approves it; the ticket book then holds exactly one more ticket, opened
#      with the trial credential, and the Task records the agent's session;
#   D. the agent proposes for the target workspace what it tried (`propose_admin_proposal`): the
#      two Skills, the Worker (never its gates or model; the system it acts on, `systems`) and
#      `tickets.create` at blast radius low in the workspace part; one http gate-host instance for the ticket system, shared credential,
#      in the platform part. The person, as platform administrator: reviews the platform part and
#      confirms its one item, applies it, waits for the gate host to announce the instance's
#      Operations (enabling it before that would pin an empty manifest), enters the production
#      credential, enables it on the platform. As the target's owner: enables the gate there (and
#      reads the ticket book through it: the production credential, no ticket opened), reviews the
#      workspace part — all four items authority_widening, each confirmed; the Worker bound to the
#      production Gatekeeper, the ticket system's one connected gate there (S11 AA5f) — and applies
#      it, which verifies the part once by itself (the production Gatekeeper probed);
#   E. the agent reads its proposal back (`agent_get_admin_proposal`): both parts applied, and —
#      like the platform's own read (`get_admin_proposal`) — nothing of the owner's dry run
#      (TICKETS_DRY_RUN_KEYS).
# Then: who did what (the agent's calls under its session; each applied item the agent's draft,
# confirmed and applied by the person; the person's calls under no session), neither credential in
# a kernel table, the production half opening no ticket, and the list of what the person had to
# do, checked against the plan's kinds: 录凭证 (twice), 试验工作区发布, 批准试验动作, 按段审阅与逐项确认
# and 每段应用 (each part), 启用门 (platform and workspace) — plus one the plan's list leaves out,
# printed as a NOTE (evidence for decision gate D-W5, AA5 plan §4 item 3): 授权门（试验）. Binding
# the Worker's gate and verifying the part are no person's steps any more (S11 AA5f): the apply
# does both.
#
# Runs only when the admin agent scenario did (its administrator signed in, its trial workspace
# set up): otherwise one `NOTE admin-agent-tickets …` line, as admin_agent_step's switch NOTE.
#
# Cleanup (admin_agent_tickets_cleanup, logged, never failed): the workspace part rolled back, then
# the platform part (its instance disabled — never deleted, so its gate id keeps its history; the
# gate host keeps the production credential for it in its encrypted store; the connector
# `accept-s2-tickets` stays, reused by the next run), or the proposal withdrawn when its platform
# part never was applied; a Worker Task still running cancelled. The rest goes with others: the
# trial gate container with cleanup_step's `rm -sf` of the accept-s2 containers, both workspaces
# disabled by admin_agent_cleanup, the ticket book with the fixture's container. The trial gate's
# data directory (its ConnectedAccount store) stays, as the other accept-s2 gates' do.

TICKETS_NONCE=""
TICKETS_CHAT_ID=""
TICKETS_SESSION_ID=""
TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID=""
TICKETS_TASK_ID=""
TICKETS_HUMAN_ACTIONS=""
TICKETS_GATE_ID=""
TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID=""
TICKETS_WS_SEGMENT_ID=""
TICKETS_PLATFORM_SEGMENT_ID=""
TICKETS_PLATFORM_CHANGE_ID=""
TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID=""
TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID=""
TICKETS_OWNER_PRINCIPAL_ID=""

# The production half's gate-host instance: the ticket system's base and its OpenAPI document (the
# openapi fixture on the control network, which gate-host shares), and the connector it joins
# (deploy/fake-llm/server.mjs TICKETS_CONNECTOR — rolling back keeps it: `accept-s2-` names it this
# script's).
TICKETS_SYSTEM_URL="http://accept-s2-openapi:8080"
TICKETS_OPENAPI_URL="http://accept-s2-openapi:8080/tickets/openapi.json"
TICKETS_CONNECTOR="accept-s2-tickets"
# Keys only an owner's dry run of a workspace part holds (preview_admin_proposal_segment and what
# applying recorded): none may appear in what the platform or the agent reads of that part.
TICKETS_DRY_RUN_KEYS="before after changedFields fields classification widening newFamily gates blockers digest unchanged targetChosen platformChanges suspectedSecretValues suspectedSecretPaths confirmedBy appliedBy decidedBy target"

# tickets_human <kind> <what>: one thing the person did, logged and kept for the list at the end.
tickets_human() {
  TICKETS_HUMAN_ACTIONS="${TICKETS_HUMAN_ACTIONS}$1
"
  echo "HUMAN admin-agent-tickets $1: $2"
}

# tickets_field <reply> <KEY>: the value of KEY=… in an agent reply (values carry no spaces).
tickets_field() {
  printf '%s' "$1" | sed -n "s/.*$2=\([^ ]*\).*/\1/p"
}

# tickets_turn <step> <chat|new:admin_agent> <text>: one admin agent Turn as the administrator in
# the trial workspace; FAILs <step> unless it completed with no tool call in error. Leaves the
# Chat in TICKETS_CHAT_ID, the tools it called in TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS and its reply in
# TICKETS_REPLY.
tickets_turn() {
  out=$(run_driver send-and-wait "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" "$2" "$3" 180000)
  TICKETS_CHAT_ID=$(parse_kv "$out" CHAT_ID)
  turn_status=$(parse_kv "$out" TURN_STATUS)
  TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS=$(parse_kv "$out" TOOL_NAMES)
  turn_errors=$(parse_kv "$out" TOOL_ERRORS)
  [ -n "$TICKETS_CHAT_ID" ] || fail "$1" "no admin agent Chat: $(printf '%s' "$out" | grep -E '^(ERROR|HTTP_STATUS|TURN_STATUS)=' | tail -3)"
  [ "$turn_status" = "completed" ] || fail "$1" "the admin agent Turn $(parse_kv "$out" TURN_ID) ended '${turn_status:-not settled within 180s}', not completed (tools: '$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS') — docker compose logs worker-supervisor"
  [ "$turn_errors" = "0" ] || fail "$1" "$turn_errors of the admin agent's calls ended in an error ($(parse_kv "$out" TOOL_ERROR_NAMES); tools: '$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS')"
  TICKETS_REPLY=$(parse_kv "$(run_driver get-history "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" "$TICKETS_CHAT_ID" "(d.filter(m=>m.role==='assistant').pop()||{}).text||''")" EXTRACTED)
  [ "$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_TOOLS)" = "ok" ] || fail "$1" "the admin container offered the wrong tools for this Turn: '$TICKETS_REPLY'"
}

# tickets_book: the ticket book as the person reads it through the gate (observe_operation
# `tickets.list` in the trial workspace) — `<count>|<JSON of the tickets titled $1>`.
tickets_book() {
  admin_cap observe_operation "{\"gatekeeperId\":\"$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID\",\"operation\":\"tickets.list\",\"params\":{}}" "(() => { const items = (d.result.data && d.result.data.items) || []; return items.length + '|' + JSON.stringify(items.filter((t) => t.title === '$1').map((t) => ({ via: t.via, priority: t.priority }))); })()" "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID"
}

admin_agent_tickets_step() {
  if [ -z "$ADMIN_SESSION" ] || [ -z "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID" ] || [ -z "$ADMIN_PRINCIPAL_ID" ]; then
    echo "NOTE admin-agent-tickets the admin agent ticket journey (connect, draft, try a Worker in the trial workspace) not run: the admin agent scenario did not run (see its NOTE above)"
    return 0
  fi
  TICKETS_NONCE=$(real_token)
  model=${ACCEPT_S2_MODEL:-fake/fake-echo}

  # The ticket system's gate, on a connection secret minted in the trial workspace.
  tickets_dir="${NEXTTIME_DATA}/accept-s2/tickets-gate"
  mkdir -p "$tickets_dir"
  chmod 777 "$tickets_dir"
  if [ ! -f "$tickets_dir/store.key" ]; then
    out=$(docker compose --profile accept-s2 run --rm --no-deps -T --entrypoint node accept-s2-tickets-gate \
      -e "require('fs').mkdirSync('/data/gate',{recursive:true});require('fs').writeFileSync('/data/gate/store.key', require('crypto').randomBytes(32));console.log('STOREKEY_OK')" \
      </dev/null 2>&1)
    case "$out" in
      *STOREKEY_OK*) : ;;
      *) fail "admin-agent-tickets-gate" "store.key generation failed: $out" ;;
    esac
  fi
  tickets_secret=$(mint_gate_secret "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" "admin-agent-tickets-gate")
  [ -n "$tickets_secret" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-gate" "mint_connection_secret in the trial workspace returned no secret"
  tickets_token_file="$tickets_dir/kernel.token"
  write_gate_secret "$tickets_secret" "$tickets_token_file" || fail "admin-agent-tickets-gate" "could not write $tickets_token_file"
  up_out=$(docker compose --profile accept-s2 up -d --force-recreate accept-s2-tickets-gate 2>&1)
  [ $? -eq 0 ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-gate" "docker compose up failed: $(printf '%s' "$up_out" | tail -20)"
  wait_for_gate_health "http://accept-s2-tickets-gate:8090" "$tickets_token_file" || fail "admin-agent-tickets-gate" "accept-s2-tickets-gate /gate/health never came back ok — docker compose logs accept-s2-tickets-gate"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-gate" "accept-s2-tickets-gate healthy on its own connection secret $(redact "$tickets_secret") (minted in the trial workspace)"

  # --- Turn A: the agent asks for the ticket system ---
  tickets_turn "admin-agent-tickets-request" new:admin_agent "验收工单：接入工单系统 TICKETS_NONCE=$TICKETS_NONCE"
  [ "$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS" = "request_connection" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-request" "the admin agent called '$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS', expected request_connection"
  cr_id=$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_CONNECTION_REQUEST)
  [ -n "$cr_id" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-request" "no connection request in the admin agent's reply: '$TICKETS_REPLY'"
  admin_cap get_admin_agent_status '{}' "(() => { const w = d.result.workspaces.find((x) => x.workspaceId === '$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID'); return w && w.session ? w.session.sessionId : ''; })()"
  TICKETS_SESSION_ID=$ADMIN_VALUE
  [ -n "$TICKETS_SESSION_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-request" "get_admin_agent_status shows no open admin agent session in the trial workspace after the Turn"
  cr_row=$(psql_ws "select kind || ',' || target || ',' || status || ',' || (requested_by = '$ADMIN_PRINCIPAL_ID')::text || ',' || coalesce(admin_agent_session_id::text, '') from connection_requests where workspace_id = '$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID' and id = '$cr_id'")
  [ "$cr_row" = "http,helpdesk,requested,true,$TICKETS_SESSION_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-request" "connection request $cr_id reads '$cr_row', expected http,helpdesk,requested,true,$TICKETS_SESSION_ID (requested by the administrator's Principal, under the admin agent's session)"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-request" "the admin agent (Chat $TICKETS_CHAT_ID) asked for an http system 'helpdesk': request $cr_id, recorded under its session $TICKETS_SESSION_ID"

  # The person completes the request: the test credential straight to the gate's store.
  out=$(cap "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" create_connection \
    "{\"connectionRequestId\":\"$cr_id\",\"kind\":\"http\",\"target\":\"helpdesk\",\"endpoint\":\"http://accept-s2-tickets-gate:8090\",\"connectionSecret\":\"$tickets_secret\",\"credentials\":{\"token\":\"$ACCEPT_S2_API_TOKEN\"},\"credentialKind\":\"connected_account\",\"manifestSource\":\"http://accept-s2-openapi:8080/tickets/openapi.json\"}" \
    "d.result.gatekeeperId")
  tickets_secret=""
  status=$(parse_kv "$out" HTTP_STATUS)
  [ "$status" = "200" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-connect" "create_connection for request $cr_id HTTP $status: $(parse_kv "$out" BODY)"
  TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID=$(parse_kv "$out" EXTRACTED)
  [ -n "$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-connect" "no gatekeeperId in response: $(parse_kv "$out" BODY)"
  tickets_human "录凭证" "create_connection for the agent's request $cr_id with the test credential (the console's request card)"
  cr_row=$(psql_ws "select status || ',' || coalesce(gatekeeper_id::text, '') || ',' || (completed_by = '$ADMIN_PRINCIPAL_ID')::text from connection_requests where workspace_id = '$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID' and id = '$cr_id'")
  [ "$cr_row" = "completed,$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID,true" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-connect" "connection request $cr_id reads '$cr_row' after create_connection, expected completed,$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID,true"
  # Not by the trial workspace exception (#954): http here is self_serve, which this script
  # requires of the S2 workspace too (connections_step).
  http_mode=$(psql_ws "select mode from connectors where name = 'http'")
  trial_self=$(psql_ws "select count(*) from audit_records where workspace_id = '$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID' and action = 'connection.trial_self_connect'")
  [ "$http_mode,$trial_self" = "self_serve,0" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-connect" "connector http is '$http_mode' with $trial_self connection.trial_self_connect audit row(s) in the trial workspace, expected self_serve and none"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-connect" "the person completed request $cr_id: Gatekeeper $TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID, credential sent to the gate (self-serve http, no trial exception used)"

  # The gate imported the OpenAPI document: two observe reads, one execute write.
  admin_cap list_operations "{\"gatekeeperId\":\"$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID\"}" "d.result.items.map((o) => o.name + ':' + o.mode).sort().join(',')" "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID"
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "tickets.create:execute,tickets.get:observe,tickets.list:observe" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-operations" "the ticket gate's Operations read '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected tickets.create:execute,tickets.get:observe,tickets.list:observe"
  out=$(publish_manifest_as_read "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" "$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID")
  status=$(parse_kv "$out" HTTP_STATUS)
  [ "$status" = "200" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-operations" "publish_manifest HTTP $status: $(parse_kv "$out" BODY)"
  tickets_human "试验工作区发布" "publish_manifest: the ticket gate's three Operations, as read"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-operations" "the gate imported the OpenAPI document as tickets.list / tickets.get (observe) and tickets.create (execute); published in the trial workspace"
  out=$(cap "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" connect_gatekeeper "{\"gatekeeperId\":\"$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID\",\"principalId\":\"$ADMIN_PRINCIPAL_ID\"}" "")
  status=$(parse_kv "$out" HTTP_STATUS)
  [ "$status" = "200" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-grant" "connect_gatekeeper HTTP $status: $(parse_kv "$out" BODY)"
  tickets_human "授权门（试验）" "connect_gatekeeper: the ticket gate granted to the administrator (the console's Systems & access page, 系统与授权)"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-grant" "the ticket gate granted to the administrator's Principal in the trial workspace"

  # --- Turn B: the agent looks and drafts ---
  tickets_turn "admin-agent-tickets-draft" "$TICKETS_CHAT_ID" "验收工单：起草工单 Worker TICKETS_NONCE=$TICKETS_NONCE WORKER_MODEL=$model"
  case "$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS" in
    find_operations,*_tickets_list,propose_skill,propose_skill,propose_worker_definition) : ;;
    *) fail "admin-agent-tickets-draft" "the admin agent called '$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS', expected find_operations, its <gate>_tickets_list tool, propose_skill twice, propose_worker_definition" ;;
  esac
  [ "$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_DRAFTED)" = "yes" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-draft" "the admin agent drafted no Worker: '$TICKETS_REPLY'"
  [ "$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_GATEKEEPER)" = "$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-draft" "find_operations led the agent to Gatekeeper '$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_GATEKEEPER)', expected $TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID"
  seen=$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_SEEN)
  case "$seen" in
    '' | *[!0-9]*) fail "admin-agent-tickets-draft" "the agent's tickets.list came back without tickets: '$TICKETS_REPLY'" ;;
  esac
  [ "$seen" -ge 2 ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-draft" "the agent saw $seen ticket(s) through tickets.list, expected the fixture's two seeded ones at least"
  skills=$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_SKILLS)
  worker=$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_WORKER)
  worker_id=${worker%%:*}
  worker_version=${worker#*:}
  [ -n "$worker_id" ] && [ -n "$worker_version" ] && [ "$worker_id" != "$worker" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-draft" "no Worker draft in the reply: '$TICKETS_REPLY'"
  skill_ids=""
  skill_count=0
  for s in $(printf '%s' "$skills" | tr ',' ' '); do
    skill_ids="$skill_ids ${s%%:*}"
    skill_count=$((skill_count + 1))
  done
  [ "$skill_count" -eq 2 ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-draft" "the reply names $skill_count Skill draft(s), expected two: '$skills'"
  for sid in $skill_ids; do
    admin_cap list_skills '{"limit":100}' "(() => { const s = d.result.items.find((x) => x.id === '$sid'); return s ? [s.status, s.origin].join(',') : 'absent'; })()" "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID"
    [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "draft,agent" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-draft" "Skill $sid reads '$ADMIN_VALUE' in the trial workspace, expected draft,agent (a private draft the agent proposed)"
  done
  admin_cap list_worker_definitions '{"kind":"worker","includeOwnDrafts":true,"limit":100}' "(() => { const w = d.result.items.find((x) => x.id === '$worker_id' && x.version === $worker_version); return w ? [w.status, w.origin, (w.definition.gates || []).join('|'), (w.definition.capabilities || []).join('|')].join(',') : 'absent'; })()" "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID"
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "draft,agent,$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID,request_action" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-draft" "WorkerDefinition $worker_id@$worker_version reads '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected draft,agent,$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID,request_action"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-draft" "the admin agent saw $seen ticket(s) through its observe tool and drafted two Skills and Worker $worker_id@$worker_version (asks for actions on the ticket gate only); all private drafts, origin agent"

  # The person publishes the three drafts in the trial workspace.
  for s in $(printf '%s' "$skills" | tr ',' ' '); do
    sid=${s%%:*}
    rest=${s#*:}
    sver=${rest%%:*}
    sdigest=${rest#*:}
    out=$(cap "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" publish_skill "{\"skillId\":\"$sid\",\"version\":$sver,\"draftDigest\":\"$sdigest\"}" "d.result.status")
    status=$(parse_kv "$out" HTTP_STATUS)
    [ "$status" = "200" ] && [ "$(parse_kv "$out" EXTRACTED)" = "published" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-publish" "publish_skill $sid@$sver HTTP $status: $(parse_kv "$out" BODY)"
    tickets_human "试验工作区发布" "publish_skill $sid@$sver (the agent's draft)"
  done
  out=$(cap "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" publish_worker_definition "{\"definitionId\":\"$worker_id\",\"version\":$worker_version}" "d.result.status")
  status=$(parse_kv "$out" HTTP_STATUS)
  [ "$status" = "200" ] && [ "$(parse_kv "$out" EXTRACTED)" = "published" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-publish" "publish_worker_definition $worker_id@$worker_version HTTP $status: $(parse_kv "$out" BODY)"
  tickets_human "试验工作区发布" "publish_worker_definition $worker_id@$worker_version (the agent's draft)"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-publish" "the person published both Skills and Worker $worker_id@$worker_version in the trial workspace"

  # --- Turn C: the agent tries the Worker ---
  tickets_book "accept-ticket-$TICKETS_NONCE"
  before=${ADMIN_VALUE%%|*}
  tickets_turn "admin-agent-tickets-try" "$TICKETS_CHAT_ID" "验收工单：试跑工单 Worker TICKETS_DEFINITION=$worker_id TICKETS_VERSION=$worker_version TICKET_TITLE=accept-ticket-$TICKETS_NONCE"
  [ "$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS" = "invoke_worker" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-try" "the admin agent called '$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS', expected invoke_worker"
  TICKETS_TASK_ID=$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_TASK_ID)
  [ -n "$TICKETS_TASK_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-try" "no Task in the admin agent's reply: '$TICKETS_REPLY'"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-try" "the admin agent started Worker $worker_id@$worker_version: Task $TICKETS_TASK_ID"

  # The Worker's tickets.create waits for a decision; the person approves it.
  ar_id=""
  attempt=0
  while [ "$attempt" -lt 60 ]; do
    out=$(cap "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" list_pending '{}' "String((((d.result.items||[]).filter(r=>r.gatekeeperId==='$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID'))[0]||{}).id||'')")
    ar_id=$(parse_kv "$out" EXTRACTED)
    [ -n "$ar_id" ] && break
    attempt=$((attempt + 1))
    sleep 2
  done
  [ -n "$ar_id" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-approve" "no ActionRequest on the ticket gate pending the person's approval within 120s of Task $TICKETS_TASK_ID — docker compose logs worker-supervisor"
  admin_cap get_action "{\"actionRequestId\":\"$ar_id\"}" "[d.result.actionKindTag, d.result.status, d.result.onBehalfOf === '$ADMIN_PRINCIPAL_ID' ? 'administrator' : 'obo:' + d.result.onBehalfOf].join(',')" "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID"
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "tickets.create,pending_approval,administrator" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-approve" "ActionRequest $ar_id reads '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected tickets.create,pending_approval,administrator"
  out=$(cap "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" approve "{\"actionRequestId\":\"$ar_id\"}" "")
  status=$(parse_kv "$out" HTTP_STATUS)
  [ "$status" = "200" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-approve" "approve $ar_id HTTP $status: $(parse_kv "$out" BODY)"
  tickets_human "批准试验动作" "approve $ar_id: the Worker's tickets.create"
  ar_status=""
  attempt=0
  while [ "$attempt" -lt 30 ]; do
    admin_cap get_action "{\"actionRequestId\":\"$ar_id\"}" "d.result.status" "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID"
    ar_status=$ADMIN_VALUE
    case "$ar_status" in executed | verified | failed | rejected | denied | expired | withdrawn | compensated) break ;; esac
    attempt=$((attempt + 1))
    sleep 2
  done
  case "$ar_status" in executed | verified) : ;; *) fail "admin-agent-tickets-approve" "ActionRequest $ar_id reads '$ar_status' after approval, expected executed — docker compose logs accept-s2-tickets-gate" ;; esac
  out=$(run_driver wait-task "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" "$TICKETS_TASK_ID" 180000)
  task_status=$(parse_kv "$out" TASK_STATUS)
  [ "$task_status" = "completed" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-approve" "Task $TICKETS_TASK_ID ended '${task_status:-not within 180s}', not completed — docker compose logs worker-supervisor"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-approve" "the person approved the Worker's tickets.create ($ar_id): $ar_status, Task $TICKETS_TASK_ID completed"

  # Exactly one more ticket, opened with the trial credential.
  tickets_book "accept-ticket-$TICKETS_NONCE"
  after=${ADMIN_VALUE%%|*}
  mine=${ADMIN_VALUE#*|}
  [ "$mine" = '[{"via":"trial","priority":"normal"}]' ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-book" "the ticket book holds '$mine' titled accept-ticket-$TICKETS_NONCE, expected one, opened with the trial credential, priority normal"
  [ "$after" -eq $((before + 1)) ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-book" "the ticket book went from $before to $after ticket(s), expected exactly one more"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-book" "the ticket book went from $before to $after: one ticket accept-ticket-$TICKETS_NONCE, opened with the trial credential"
  ar_count=$(psql_ws "select count(*) from action_requests where workspace_id = '$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID' and gatekeeper_id = '$TICKETS_GATEKEEPER_ID'")
  [ "$ar_count" = "1" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-book" "$ar_count ActionRequest(s) on the ticket gate, expected the one approved"

  # The Task records the agent's session; the session did not change across the three Turns.
  task_row=$(psql_ws "select status || ',' || (on_behalf_of = '$ADMIN_PRINCIPAL_ID')::text || ',' || coalesce(admin_agent_session_id::text, '') from tasks where workspace_id = '$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID' and id = '$TICKETS_TASK_ID'")
  [ "$task_row" = "completed,true,$TICKETS_SESSION_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-task" "Task $TICKETS_TASK_ID reads '$task_row', expected completed,true,$TICKETS_SESSION_ID (for the administrator, under the admin agent's session)"
  admin_cap get_admin_agent_status '{}' "(() => { const w = d.result.workspaces.find((x) => x.workspaceId === '$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID'); return w && w.session ? w.session.sessionId : ''; })()"
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "$TICKETS_SESSION_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-task" "the admin agent's session is now '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected the same $TICKETS_SESSION_ID across the three Turns"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-task" "Task $TICKETS_TASK_ID: for the administrator, recorded under the admin agent's session $TICKETS_SESSION_ID"

  # === The production half (AA5 plan §5.8, 提议 / 应用) ===
  # --- Turn D: the agent proposes what it tried, for the target workspace ---
  TICKETS_GATE_ID="accept-tickets-$TICKETS_NONCE"
  tickets_turn "admin-agent-tickets-propose" "$TICKETS_CHAT_ID" "验收工单：提议接入正式工作区 TICKETS_NONCE=$TICKETS_NONCE TICKETS_WORKSPACE=$ADMIN_TARGET_ID TICKETS_SYSTEM=$TICKETS_SYSTEM_URL TICKETS_OPENAPI=$TICKETS_OPENAPI_URL"
  [ "$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS" = "agent_list_proposal_targets,propose_admin_proposal" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-propose" "the admin agent called '$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS', expected agent_list_proposal_targets,propose_admin_proposal"
  TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID=$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID)
  [ -n "$TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-propose" "no proposal in the admin agent's reply: '$TICKETS_REPLY'"
  [ "$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_PROPOSAL_STATUS)" = "proposed" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-propose" "proposal $TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID came back '$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_PROPOSAL_STATUS)', expected proposed"
  [ "$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_ADDRESS_WITHHELD)" = "yes" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-propose" "the agent read its gate-host instance back with its addresses: '$TICKETS_REPLY'"
  admin_cap get_admin_proposal "{\"proposalId\":\"$TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID\"}" "d.result.segments.map((s) => [s.authority, s.status, s.targetWorkspaceId || '-', s.items.map((i) => i.kind + (i.systems ? '[' + i.systems.join('+') + ']' : '')).join('+')].join(':')).join(',')"
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "workspace:proposed:$ADMIN_TARGET_ID:skill_version+skill_version+worker_definition_version[$TICKETS_CONNECTOR]+operation_version,platform:proposed:-:gate_instance" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-propose" "proposal $TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID reads '$ADMIN_VALUE' on the platform, expected a workspace part for $ADMIN_TARGET_ID (two Skills, the Worker naming the system $TICKETS_CONNECTOR, one Operation) and a platform part (one gate-host instance), both proposed"
  admin_cap get_admin_proposal "{\"proposalId\":\"$TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID\"}" "d.result.segments.find((s) => s.authority === 'workspace').id + ',' + d.result.segments.find((s) => s.authority === 'platform').id"
  TICKETS_WS_SEGMENT_ID=${ADMIN_VALUE%%,*}
  TICKETS_PLATFORM_SEGMENT_ID=${ADMIN_VALUE#*,}
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-propose" "the admin agent proposed $TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID: for $ADMIN_TARGET_ID the two Skills and the Worker it tried and tickets.create at blast radius low; on the platform a gate-host instance $TICKETS_GATE_ID (read back to the agent without its addresses)"

  # --- The platform part: a platform administrator reviews, confirms and applies it ---
  admin_cap preview_platform_segment "{\"segmentId\":\"$TICKETS_PLATFORM_SEGMENT_ID\"}" "[d.result.blockers.length, d.result.suspectedSecretValues, d.result.items.map((i) => [i.ordinal, i.gateId, i.connector.name, i.classification, i.widening.map((w) => w.path + '/' + w.reason).join('+')].join(':')).join(','), d.result.digest].join('|')"
  case "$ADMIN_VALUE" in
    "0|0|1:$TICKETS_GATE_ID:$TICKETS_CONNECTOR:authority_widening:target/added|sha256:"*) : ;;
    *) fail "admin-agent-tickets-platform" "preview_platform_segment reads '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected no blocker, no suspected credential, one authority_widening instance $TICKETS_GATE_ID on connector $TICKETS_CONNECTOR, and a digest" ;;
  esac
  platform_digest=${ADMIN_VALUE##*|}
  tickets_human "按段审阅与逐项确认" "preview_platform_segment $TICKETS_PLATFORM_SEGMENT_ID: the gate-host instance, confirmed by its ordinal"
  admin_cap apply_platform_segment "{\"segmentId\":\"$TICKETS_PLATFORM_SEGMENT_ID\",\"reviewedDigest\":\"$platform_digest\",\"confirmedOrdinals\":[1]}" "[d.result.segment.status, d.result.changeSegment.id, d.result.changeSegment.items.map((i) => i.gateId).join('+')].join(',')"
  TICKETS_PLATFORM_CHANGE_ID=$(printf '%s' "$ADMIN_VALUE" | cut -d, -f2)
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "applied,$TICKETS_PLATFORM_CHANGE_ID,$TICKETS_GATE_ID" ] && [ -n "$TICKETS_PLATFORM_CHANGE_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-platform" "apply_platform_segment reads '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected applied, its change segment and $TICKETS_GATE_ID"
  tickets_human "每段应用" "apply_platform_segment $TICKETS_PLATFORM_SEGMENT_ID"

  # The gate host announces it (its pull interval, 60 s by default) — waited for before the
  # instance is enabled: enabling first would pin an empty manifest (the announced Operations then
  # wait in pendingManifest for a platform administrator to confirm).
  gate_state=""
  attempt=0
  while [ "$attempt" -lt 60 ]; do
    admin_cap get_gate_instance "{\"gateId\":\"$TICKETS_GATE_ID\"}" "[d.result.status, d.result.lastSeenAt ? 'seen' : 'unseen', d.result.operationCount, d.result.operations.map((o) => o.name + ':' + o.mode + ':' + o.blastRadius).sort().join('+')].join(',')"
    gate_state=$ADMIN_VALUE
    case "$gate_state" in discovered,seen,3,*) break ;; esac
    attempt=$((attempt + 1))
    sleep 5
  done
  [ "$gate_state" = "discovered,seen,3,tickets.create:execute:medium+tickets.get:observe:low+tickets.list:observe:low" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-platform" "gate-host instance $TICKETS_GATE_ID reads '$gate_state' 300s after the apply, expected discovered, announced, with tickets.create (execute, medium) and tickets.get / tickets.list (observe, low) — docker compose logs gate-host"

  # The production credential: the console's 集成 page, straight to the gate host (the kernel never
  # sees it). The gate host takes it once its pull has the instance (404 until then).
  post_status=""
  attempt=0
  while [ "$attempt" -lt 12 ]; do
    out=$(run_driver gate-host-credential "$(admin_cred)" "$TICKETS_GATE_ID" "{\"token\":\"$ACCEPT_S2_TICKETS_PROD_TOKEN\"}")
    post_status=$(parse_kv "$out" POST_STATUS)
    [ "$post_status" = "404" ] || break
    attempt=$((attempt + 1))
    sleep 5
  done
  [ "$(parse_kv "$out" TOKEN_STATUS),$(parse_kv "$out" CREDENTIAL_MODE),$post_status" = "200,shared,200" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-platform" "entering the production credential: issue_gate_host_token HTTP $(parse_kv "$out" TOKEN_STATUS) (mode '$(parse_kv "$out" CREDENTIAL_MODE)'), gate host HTTP '$post_status' $(parse_kv "$out" POST_ERROR) — docker compose logs gate-host"
  tickets_human "录凭证" "the production credential for $TICKETS_GATE_ID, to the gate host (the console's 集成 page)"
  admin_cap update_gate_instance "{\"gateId\":\"$TICKETS_GATE_ID\",\"status\":\"enabled\"}" "d.result.status"
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "enabled" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-platform" "update_gate_instance $TICKETS_GATE_ID answered status '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected enabled"
  tickets_human "启用门" "update_gate_instance $TICKETS_GATE_ID enabled (platform)"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-platform" "the platform part applied (change segment $TICKETS_PLATFORM_CHANGE_ID): $TICKETS_GATE_ID announced its three Operations as imported, took the production credential and was enabled on the platform"

  # --- The workspace part: the owner enables the gate, reviews, confirms and applies ---
  TICKETS_OWNER_PRINCIPAL_ID=$(psql_ws "select id from principals where workspace_id='$ADMIN_TARGET_ID' and user_id='$ADMIN_USER_ID' and kind='human'")
  [ -n "$TICKETS_OWNER_PRINCIPAL_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-enable" "no Principal of $ADMIN_USER_ID in the target workspace $ADMIN_TARGET_ID"
  admin_cap preview_gate_instance_enable "{\"gateId\":\"$TICKETS_GATE_ID\"}" "[d.result.wouldLink === null, d.result.awaitingPlatformAdoption === null, d.result.operationsToImport.map((o) => o.name).sort().join('+'), d.result.manifestDigest].join(',')" "$ADMIN_TARGET_ID"
  case "$ADMIN_VALUE" in
    "true,true,tickets.create+tickets.get+tickets.list,"?*) : ;;
    *) fail "admin-agent-tickets-enable" "preview_gate_instance_enable in $ADMIN_TARGET_ID reads '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected a new link, nothing awaiting the platform, the three Operations to import and a manifest digest" ;;
  esac
  out=$(cap "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TARGET_ID")" enable_gate_instance "{\"gateId\":\"$TICKETS_GATE_ID\",\"manifestDigest\":\"${ADMIN_VALUE##*,}\"}" "[d.result.gatekeeperId, [...d.result.publishedOperationNames].sort().join('+')].join(',')")
  status=$(parse_kv "$out" HTTP_STATUS)
  [ "$status" = "200" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-enable" "enable_gate_instance $TICKETS_GATE_ID in $ADMIN_TARGET_ID HTTP $status: $(parse_kv "$out" BODY)"
  TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID=$(parse_kv "$out" EXTRACTED)
  TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID=${TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID%%,*}
  [ "$(parse_kv "$out" EXTRACTED)" = "$TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID,tickets.create+tickets.get+tickets.list" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-enable" "enable_gate_instance answered '$(parse_kv "$out" EXTRACTED)', expected a Gatekeeper and the three Operations published"
  tickets_human "启用门" "enable_gate_instance $TICKETS_GATE_ID in $ADMIN_TARGET_ID (workspace)"
  # The production gate reads the ticket book with the production credential — and writes nothing.
  admin_cap observe_operation "{\"gatekeeperId\":\"$TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID\",\"operation\":\"tickets.list\",\"params\":{}}" "[(d.result.data && d.result.data.readBy) || '', ((d.result.data && d.result.data.items) || []).length].join(',')" "$ADMIN_TARGET_ID"
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "production,$after" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-enable" "tickets.list through the production gate reads '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected production,$after (read with the production credential; the trial's ticket the last one)"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-enable" "the owner enabled $TICKETS_GATE_ID in $ADMIN_TARGET_ID (Gatekeeper $TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID); through it the ticket system answers the production credential"

  # S11 AA5f: the Worker names the ticket system, has no gates here yet, so the apply binds it to
  # the system's connected gates here — the production Gatekeeper alone, which the owner does not
  # hold (enabling a gate grants nobody; the binding grants nothing either).
  admin_cap preview_admin_proposal_segment "{\"segmentId\":\"$TICKETS_WS_SEGMENT_ID\"}" "[d.result.blockers.length, d.result.targetChosen, d.result.suspectedSecretValues, d.result.items.map((i) => [i.ordinal, i.kind, i.classification, i.widening.map((w) => w.path + '/' + w.reason).join('+')].join(':')).join(','), (() => { const w = d.result.items.find((i) => i.kind === 'worker_definition_version'); return w ? [w.gateBinding.source, w.gateBinding.systems.join('+'), w.gateBinding.candidates.map((c) => c.id + '/' + c.connector + '/' + c.held).join('+'), w.gates.map((g) => g.id).join('+')].join(':') : 'absent'; })(), d.result.digest].join('|')" "$ADMIN_TARGET_ID"
  case "$ADMIN_VALUE" in
    "0|true|0|1:skill_version:authority_widening:skill/added,2:skill_version:authority_widening:skill/added,3:worker_definition_version:authority_widening:worker/added,4:operation_version:authority_widening:operation.blast_radius/loosened|apply:$TICKETS_CONNECTOR:$TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID/$TICKETS_CONNECTOR/false:$TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID|sha256:"*) : ;;
    *) fail "admin-agent-tickets-apply" "preview_admin_proposal_segment in $ADMIN_TARGET_ID reads '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected no blocker, still a chosen target, no suspected credential, four authority_widening items (two Skills and the Worker added, tickets.create's blast radius loosened), the Worker bound by this apply to $TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID (the one connected gate of $TICKETS_CONNECTOR here, not held by the owner) and a digest" ;;
  esac
  ws_digest=${ADMIN_VALUE##*|}
  tickets_human "按段审阅与逐项确认" "preview_admin_proposal_segment $TICKETS_WS_SEGMENT_ID: four items, each confirmed by its ordinal"
  # S11 AA5f: right after it commits, the apply verifies the part once as the owner (trigger
  # system) — legacy 630's probe of the gates what it wrote runs through: here only the production
  # Gatekeeper (tickets.create's blast radius lives there, and the Worker is bound to it).
  admin_cap apply_admin_proposal_segment "{\"segmentId\":\"$TICKETS_WS_SEGMENT_ID\",\"reviewedDigest\":\"$ws_digest\",\"confirmedOrdinals\":[1,2,3,4]}" "[d.result.segment.status, d.result.changeSegmentId, (() => { const v = d.result.verification; return v ? [v.trigger, v.passed, v.items.map((i) => i.state).join('+'), v.requirements.map((r) => [r.connector, r.state, r.met, r.gates.map((g) => g.id + '/' + g.health).join('+')].join(':')).join(';')].join('|') : 'null'; })()].join(',')" "$ADMIN_TARGET_ID"
  apply_rest=${ADMIN_VALUE#*,}
  TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID=${apply_rest%%,*}
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "applied,$TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID,system|true|in_effect+in_effect+in_effect+in_effect|$TICKETS_CONNECTOR:connected:true:$TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID/ok" ] && [ -n "$TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-apply" "apply_admin_proposal_segment reads '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected applied, its change segment, and the verification it ran: trigger system, passed, the four items in effect and one requirement — $TICKETS_CONNECTOR connected and met, its production Gatekeeper probed ok"
  tickets_human "每段应用" "apply_admin_proposal_segment $TICKETS_WS_SEGMENT_ID in $ADMIN_TARGET_ID"
  admin_cap get_change_segment "{\"segmentId\":\"$TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID\"}" "[d.result.segment.status, d.result.verification ? d.result.verification.trigger : 'none'].join(',')" "$ADMIN_TARGET_ID"
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "verified,system" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-apply" "get_change_segment $TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID reads '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected verified by the apply's own run (trigger system)"
  # What applying wrote: the Worker bound to the production Gatekeeper (a proposal never sets a
  # gate: the apply bound the one the owner kept), tickets.create at blast radius low and still
  # approved one by one.
  admin_cap list_worker_definitions '{"kind":"worker","limit":100}' "(() => { const w = d.result.items.find((x) => x.definition.name === 'accept-tickets-worker-$TICKETS_NONCE'); return w ? [w.status, w.origin, (w.definition.gates || []).join('+'), (w.definition.capabilities || []).join('|')].join(',') : 'absent'; })()" "$ADMIN_TARGET_ID"
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "published,agent,$TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID,request_action" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-apply" "the Worker in $ADMIN_TARGET_ID reads '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected published, origin agent, its one gate $TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID, request_action"
  admin_cap list_operations "{\"gatekeeperId\":\"$TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID\"}" "(() => { const o = d.result.items.filter((x) => x.name === 'tickets.create' && x.status === 'published').sort((a, b) => b.version - a.version)[0]; return o ? [o.status, o.mode, o.blastRadius, o.autoApprovable].join(',') : 'absent'; })()" "$ADMIN_TARGET_ID"
  [ "$ADMIN_VALUE" = "published,execute,low,false" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-apply" "tickets.create in $ADMIN_TARGET_ID reads '$ADMIN_VALUE', expected published, execute, blast radius low, still not auto-approvable"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-apply" "the owner applied the workspace part (change segment $TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID, four items confirmed one by one), which verified it by itself; the Worker is published bound to $TICKETS_PROD_GATEKEEPER_ID, tickets.create is low and still not auto-approvable"

  # --- What the platform and the agent read of the workspace part: the proposal, never the dry run ---
  admin_cap get_admin_proposal "{\"proposalId\":\"$TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID\"}" "(() => { const keys = new Set(); const walk = (v) => { if (Array.isArray(v)) v.forEach(walk); else if (v && typeof v === 'object') for (const [k, x] of Object.entries(v)) { keys.add(k); walk(x); } }; walk(d.result.segments.filter((s) => s.authority === 'workspace')); return d.result.segments.map((s) => s.authority + ':' + s.status).join(',') + ' ' + [...keys].sort().join('|'); })()"
  platform_view=$ADMIN_VALUE
  [ "${platform_view%% *}" = "workspace:applied,platform:applied" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-reads" "the platform reads proposal $TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID as '${platform_view%% *}', expected both parts applied"
  tickets_turn "admin-agent-tickets-reads" "$TICKETS_CHAT_ID" "验收工单：查看提案进展 TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID=$TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID"
  [ "$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS" = "agent_get_admin_proposal" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-reads" "the admin agent called '$TICKETS_TURN_TOOLS', expected agent_get_admin_proposal"
  [ "$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_AGENT_STATUSES)" = "workspace:applied,platform:applied" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-reads" "the agent reads its proposal as '$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_AGENT_STATUSES)', expected both parts applied"
  agent_keys=$(tickets_field "$TICKETS_REPLY" TICKETS_AGENT_KEYS)
  for plane in platform agent; do
    if [ "$plane" = "platform" ]; then keys=${platform_view#* }; else keys=$agent_keys; fi
    [ -n "$keys" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-reads" "the $plane read of proposal $TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID came back empty"
    for k in $TICKETS_DRY_RUN_KEYS; do
      case "|$keys|" in *"|$k|"*) fail "admin-agent-tickets-reads" "the $plane read of proposal $TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID carries '$k', which only the owner's dry run holds: $keys" ;; esac
    done
  done
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-reads" "the platform and the agent read both parts applied, and nothing of the owner's dry run ($(printf '%s' "$TICKETS_DRY_RUN_KEYS" | tr ' ' ','))"

  # Who did what: the agent's calls under its session, the person's under none. The scenario
  # before this one proposed in the same trial workspace and session, so only this journey's
  # proposal counts.
  agent_rows=$(psql_ws "select string_agg(action, ',' order by action) from audit_records where workspace_id = '$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID' and actor_principal_id = '$ADMIN_PRINCIPAL_ID' and payload->>'sessionKind' = 'admin_agent' and payload->>'sessionId' = '$TICKETS_SESSION_ID' and action in ('request_connection', 'propose_skill', 'propose_worker_definition', 'invoke_worker', 'propose_admin_proposal') and (action <> 'propose_admin_proposal' or resource_id = '$TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID')")
  [ "$agent_rows" = "invoke_worker,propose_admin_proposal,propose_skill,propose_skill,propose_worker_definition,request_connection" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-audit" "the agent's audit rows under its session read '$agent_rows', expected invoke_worker,propose_admin_proposal,propose_skill,propose_skill,propose_worker_definition,request_connection"
  person_rows=$(psql_ws "select string_agg(action || ':' || coalesce(payload->>'sessionKind', 'person'), ',' order by action) from audit_records where workspace_id = '$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID' and actor_principal_id = '$ADMIN_PRINCIPAL_ID' and action in ('create_connection', 'publish_skill', 'publish_worker_definition')")
  [ "$person_rows" = "create_connection:person,publish_skill:person,publish_skill:person,publish_worker_definition:person" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-audit" "the person's audit rows read '$person_rows', expected create_connection, publish_skill twice and publish_worker_definition, none under a session"
  approve_row=$(psql_ws "select string_agg(coalesce(payload->>'sessionKind', 'person'), ',') from audit_records where workspace_id = '$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID' and actor_principal_id = '$ADMIN_PRINCIPAL_ID' and action = 'action_request.approve' and resource_id = '$ar_id'")
  [ "$approve_row" = "person" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-audit" "the approval of $ar_id reads '$approve_row', expected one row by the administrator's Principal under no session"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-audit" "audit: the agent's request, drafts and try under its session; the credential, the publishing and the approval by the person, under none"

  # The production half (I-A7): the proposal drafted by the agent (above, under its session); each
  # applied item recorded as the agent's draft, confirmed and applied by the person; the platform
  # part applied by the person, for the administrator whose agent proposed it.
  item_rows=$(psql_ws "select string_agg(payload->>'ordinal' || ':' || coalesce(payload->>'origin', '-') || ':' || coalesce(payload->'adminProposal'->>'proposedByUser', '-') || ':' || (coalesce(payload->>'confirmedBy', '-') = '$TICKETS_OWNER_PRINCIPAL_ID')::text || ':' || (actor_principal_id = '$TICKETS_OWNER_PRINCIPAL_ID')::text || ':' || coalesce(payload->>'sessionKind', 'person'), ',' order by (payload->>'ordinal')::int) from audit_records where workspace_id = '$ADMIN_TARGET_ID' and action = 'change_item.apply' and payload->>'segmentId' = '$TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID'")
  expected=""
  for n in 1 2 3 4; do expected="${expected:+$expected,}$n:agent:$ADMIN_USER_ID:true:true:person"; done
  [ "$item_rows" = "$expected" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-audit" "the applied items' audit rows in $ADMIN_TARGET_ID read '$item_rows', expected $expected (drafted by the agent of $ADMIN_USER_ID, confirmed and applied by the owner, under no session)"
  # enable_gate_instance's row names its gate only in the call's params (dispatch's audit copy).
  # The apply's own verification (S11 AA5f) is the verify row, as the owner's run with trigger
  # system; nobody called verify_change_segment.
  apply_rows=$(psql_ws "select string_agg(action || ':' || (actor_principal_id = '$TICKETS_OWNER_PRINCIPAL_ID')::text || ':' || coalesce(payload->>'sessionKind', 'person') || ':' || coalesce(payload->>'trigger', '-'), ',' order by action) from audit_records where workspace_id = '$ADMIN_TARGET_ID' and ((action = 'apply_admin_proposal_segment' and payload->>'proposalId' = '$TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID') or (action = 'enable_gate_instance' and payload->'params'->>'gateId' = '$TICKETS_GATE_ID') or (action in ('verify_change_segment', 'change_segment.verify') and resource_id = '$TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID'))")
  [ "$apply_rows" = "apply_admin_proposal_segment:true:person:-,change_segment.verify:true:person:system,enable_gate_instance:true:person:-" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-audit" "the owner's apply, verify and enable rows in $ADMIN_TARGET_ID read '$apply_rows', expected one each, by the owner under no session, the verification the apply's own (trigger system)"
  platform_rows=$(psql_ws "select string_agg(action || ':' || (actor_user_id = '$ADMIN_USER_ID')::text || ':' || coalesce(payload->>'sessionKind', 'person') || ':' || coalesce(payload->>'proposedByUser', '-'), ',' order by action) from audit_records where workspace_id is null and action = 'apply_platform_segment' and payload->>'proposalId' = '$TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID'")
  [ "$platform_rows" = "apply_platform_segment:true:person:$ADMIN_USER_ID" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-audit" "the platform part's apply row reads '$platform_rows', expected one by the administrator under no session, recording $ADMIN_USER_ID as whose agent proposed it"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-audit-production" "audit: the proposal under the agent's session; four applied items marked origin agent, proposed for $ADMIN_USER_ID, confirmed and applied by the owner; the platform part applied by the administrator — none of the person's rows under a session"

  # Neither credential is in a kernel table.
  token_rows_in_kernel_db "$ACCEPT_S2_API_TOKEN" || fail "admin-agent-tickets-no-token-leak" "$TOKEN_ROWS_ERROR"
  [ "$TOKEN_ROWS" = "0" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-no-token-leak" "the trial credential found in $TOKEN_ROWS row(s) across kernel DB tables"
  token_rows_in_kernel_db "$ACCEPT_S2_TICKETS_PROD_TOKEN" || fail "admin-agent-tickets-no-token-leak" "$TOKEN_ROWS_ERROR"
  [ "$TOKEN_ROWS" = "0" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-no-token-leak" "the production credential found in $TOKEN_ROWS row(s) across kernel DB tables"
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-no-token-leak" "the trial and the production credential each appear in 0 rows across all $TOKEN_ROWS_TABLES public tables"

  # The production half opened no ticket.
  tickets_book "accept-ticket-$TICKETS_NONCE"
  [ "${ADMIN_VALUE%%|*}" = "$after" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-book" "the ticket book went from $after to ${ADMIN_VALUE%%|*} ticket(s) during the production half, expected none opened"

  # What the person had to do, against the plan's kinds (§5.8): 录凭证 twice (trial, production),
  # 试验工作区发布, 批准试验动作, 按段审阅与逐项确认 and 每段应用 for each part, 启用门 in both places.
  extra=""
  for kind in $(printf '%s' "$TICKETS_HUMAN_ACTIONS" | sort -u); do
    case "$kind" in
      录凭证 | 试验工作区发布 | 批准试验动作 | 按段审阅与逐项确认 | 每段应用 | 启用门) : ;;
      授权门（试验）) extra="${extra:+$extra }$kind" ;;
      *) fail "admin-agent-tickets-human" "the person did '$kind', not one of the plan's kinds (录凭证, 试验工作区发布, 批准试验动作, 按段审阅与逐项确认, 每段应用, 启用门)" ;;
    esac
  done
  for kind in 录凭证 按段审阅与逐项确认 每段应用 启用门; do
    n=$(printf '%s' "$TICKETS_HUMAN_ACTIONS" | grep -cx "$kind")
    [ "$n" = "2" ] || fail "admin-agent-tickets-human" "the person did $kind $n time(s), expected twice (the plan: 录凭证 for each credential, each of the two parts reviewed and applied, the gate enabled on the platform and in the workspace)"
  done
  summary=$(printf '%s' "$TICKETS_HUMAN_ACTIONS" | sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^ *\([0-9]*\) \(.*\)$/\2×\1/' | tr '\n' ' ')
  pass "admin-agent-tickets-human" "what the person did: $summary"
  for kind in $extra; do
    case "$kind" in
      授权门（试验）) echo "NOTE admin-agent-tickets $kind is a person's step the AA5 plan's §5.8 list leaves out: the Worker asks for actions only on gates its person holds (connect_gatekeeper on Systems & access, 系统与授权) — D-W5 evidence (AA5 plan §4 item 3)" ;;
    esac
  done
}

# Logged, never failed (header): the production half rolled back — the workspace part first (its
# platform part refuses while one is applied), then the platform part, or the proposal withdrawn
# when its platform part never was applied; a Task still running is cancelled; everything else
# goes with cleanup_step's `rm -sf` and admin_agent_cleanup.
admin_agent_tickets_cleanup() {
  [ -n "$ADMIN_SESSION" ] || return 0
  if [ -n "$TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID" ] && [ -n "$ADMIN_TARGET_ID" ]; then
    out=$(cap "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TARGET_ID")" preview_roll_back_change_segment "{\"segmentId\":\"$TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID\"}" "JSON.stringify(d.result.items.filter((i) => i.classification === 'authority_widening').map((i) => i.ordinal))")
    confirmed=$(parse_kv "$out" EXTRACTED)
    out=$(cap "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TARGET_ID")" roll_back_change_segment "{\"segmentId\":\"$TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID\",\"confirmedOrdinals\":${confirmed:-[]}}" "d.result.status")
    echo "cleanup: roll_back_change_segment $TICKETS_CHANGE_SEGMENT_ID in $ADMIN_TARGET_ID HTTP $(parse_kv "$out" HTTP_STATUS) ($(parse_kv "$out" EXTRACTED))"
  fi
  if [ -n "$TICKETS_PLATFORM_CHANGE_ID" ]; then
    out=$(cap "$(admin_cred)" roll_back_platform_change_segment "{\"changeSegmentId\":\"$TICKETS_PLATFORM_CHANGE_ID\"}" "d.result.changeSegment.status")
    echo "cleanup: roll_back_platform_change_segment $TICKETS_PLATFORM_CHANGE_ID HTTP $(parse_kv "$out" HTTP_STATUS) ($(parse_kv "$out" EXTRACTED)) — gate-host instance $TICKETS_GATE_ID disabled, connector $TICKETS_CONNECTOR kept"
  elif [ -n "$TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID" ]; then
    out=$(cap "$(admin_cred)" withdraw_admin_proposal "{\"proposalId\":\"$TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID\",\"reason\":\"accept_s2 ticket journey: cleanup\"}")
    echo "cleanup: withdraw_admin_proposal $TICKETS_PROPOSAL_ID HTTP $(parse_kv "$out" HTTP_STATUS)"
  fi
  [ -n "$TICKETS_TASK_ID" ] && [ -n "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID" ] || return 0
  out=$(cap "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" get_task "{\"taskId\":\"$TICKETS_TASK_ID\"}" "d.result.status")
  task_status=$(parse_kv "$out" EXTRACTED)
  case "$task_status" in
    completed | failed | cancelled) echo "cleanup: ticket journey Task $TICKETS_TASK_ID already $task_status" ;;
    *)
      out=$(cap "$(admin_cred "$ADMIN_TRIAL_ID")" cancel_task "{\"taskId\":\"$TICKETS_TASK_ID\"}" "")
      echo "cleanup: cancel_task $TICKETS_TASK_ID (was '${task_status:-unread}') HTTP $(parse_kv "$out" HTTP_STATUS)"
      ;;
  esac
}
